{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will make you a great nation.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that the road brings about three things: it diminishes fertility, it diminishes wealth, and it diminishes one's reputation. Therefore He assured him with these three blessings. ״ואעשך לגוי גדול״ — this is fertility; ״ואברכך״ — this is the blessing of wealth; ״ואגדלה שמך״ — corresponding to the diminishing of reputation. It is not written אשימך here but rather ואעשך: 'I am making you a new creation,' in the manner of what is said (Genesis 1:7): ״ויעש אלהים את הרקיע״. ״לגוי גדול״ — these are Israel, of whom it is written (Deuteronomy 4:8): ״ומי גוי גדול״. ״ואעשך לגוי גדול״ — this is the one who says 'Elohei Avraham.' ״ואברכך״ — this is the one who says 'Elohei Yitzchak.' ״ואגדלה שמך״ — this is the one who says 'Elohei Yaakov.' ״והיה ברכה״ — 'in you they conclude,' and not in all of them. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: When I created My world I needed to bless My creatures — I blessed Adam and Chavah, as it says (Genesis 1:1): ״ויברך אותם אלהים״; I blessed Noach and his sons, as it says: ״ויברך אלהים את נח ואת בניו״. From here onward — ״והיה ברכה״: the blessings are given over to you to bless whomever you wish."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:48.647663546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}